abstract: "Geodesic hyperbolic sliced Wasserstein distance (Bonet et al. 2023) extends, with no moment assumption, to a metric whose completion is the space of probability measures on the compact closed Klein ball; it metrises weak convergence there and has exact diameter 2C_{d,p}^{1/p}. Exact radial rates show it is exponentially insensitive to depth; the induced boundary-sphere metric is computed in every dimension; the vanishing-at-infinity assertion of Bonet, Drumetz and Courty (JMLR 2025, Prop. 19) is corrected by an explicit function; distribution-free optimal estimation rates hold in expectation and with high probability; one radial term gives a complete metric with the hyperbolic Wasserstein topology. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
